.TH hollywood 1 "16 November 2026" hollywood "hollywood"
.SH NAME
hollywood \- fill your console with Hollywood melodrama technobabble

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhollywood\fP [-s|--splits SPLITS] [-d|--delay DELAY] [-V|--version]

.SH OPTIONS

    -d|--delay DELAY        The delay in seconds before rearranging splits (default=10s)
    -s|--splits SPLITS      The number of splits to divide your screen (default=2*nproc, capped at available widgets)
    -V|--version            Print the version and exit

.SH DESCRIPTION

This utility will fill your console with Hollywood melodrama technobabble.

It will split your \fBtmux\fP(1) or \fBbyobu\fP(1) console into a multiple panes of genuine technobabble, perfectly suitable for any Hollywood geek melodrama.

It is particularly suitable on any number of computer consoles in the background of any excellent schlock technothriller.

While the show runs, one pane at a time gets another widget, in place; the layout, the sizes and the selection stay.  A toolbar at the bottom holds every control as a button.  Click a pane to select it, double click it or press \fBz\fP to zoom it, right click it for a menu, drag a border to resize.  \fBs\fP puts another widget into the selected pane; \fBk\fP keeps the pane as it is, and lets it go again; \fBx\fP closes it and keeps its widget away for the rest of the show; \fBa\fP opens a widget of your choice; \fBr\fP allows closed widgets again; \fB+\fP and \fB-\fP add and remove one pane; \fBp\fP or space pauses and resumes the swapping; \fBn\fP builds the whole screen anew; \fB?\fP shows the keys; \fBq\fP quits.  With \fB-r\fP the whole screen is built anew every \fB-d\fP seconds, as upstream does.  These controls exist in the tmux session that \fBhollywood\fP creates itself, not in a session it was started in; the clickable toolbar needs tmux 3.4 or newer.

To quit, press q or Ctrl-C in any pane.

\fBhollywood\fP tries not to overwhelm your system by running widgets with the minimum scheduling priority per \fBnice\fP(1).

.SH SECURITY NOTE

Some \fBhollywood\fP widgets display real system information such as running processes, log files, network interface statistics, and file system details.  This information could be sensitive in some environments.

For demonstrations or presentations, check what the panes show before you share your screen.

.SH MACOS

On macOS, programs that Homebrew does not ship (\fBccze\fP, \fBapg\fP, \fBspeedometer\fP, \fBatop\fP) are replaced by small stand-ins from \fIshare/hollywood/shims\fP.  A real installation found in PATH always wins.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtmux\fP(1), \fBbyobu\fP(1), \fBnice\fP(1), https://hollywood.celox.io

